CLAIM AUDIT:

"Hundreds of Indigenous delegates have gathered in Geneva for the 19th annual session of EMRIP" â€” source: "hundreds of Indigenous delegates gather in Geneva at the 19th annual gathering." Verified.

Dhamai quote: "Climate change, militarization, extractivism, and legal marginalization reinforce one another" â€” reproduced accurately. Verified.

Toki: "lose-lose situation for Indigenous peoples on all fronts" â€” accurately attributed. Verified.

"battered by record-breaking storms, dried out by drought, and submerged by rising seas" â€” faithful paraphrase of the source's "battered by record-breaking storms, dessicated by drought, and vanishing under rising seas." Verified.

"hundreds of Indigenous people continue dying in wars and while defending their lands, even as they are persecuted by government officials" â€” source text matches. Verified.

Breathing Lands, Ring of Fire mineral deposit, nickel and other metals, 49 communities â€” all drawn directly from source. Verified.

Mattinas co-founded Okiniwak â€” source: "Mattinas is also the co-founder of Okiniwak." The founding year of 2025 present in the source is omitted from the draft; this is an omission, not an error. Verified.

Canadian legislation allowing projects "advanced through an accelerated process" â€” source quote reproduced with quotation marks intact. Verified.

Cooper: Indigenous Nama from Botswana, faces forced assimilation and displacement â€” source verified.

Xulue: "170 years of colonization" â€” exact figure from source. Verified.

ICJ advisory opinion holding climate-contributing countries accountable â€” source: "an International Court of Justice advisory opinion that said the countries contributing to climate change are accountable for the damage it has caused." Accurate summary. Verified.

Mattinas quote in the final section â€” transcribed accurately from source. Verified.

"approaching 20th anniversary of UNDRIP" â€” source: "the approaching 20th anniversary of UNDRIP next year." Accurate. Verified.

"central question... not whether Indigenous rights should be recognized, but whether governments are prepared to uphold them" â€” source text matches. Verified.

No unsupported numbers, invented actors, or fabricated causal mechanisms found.

